{"parentUuid":"b40734c0-2c36-46f3-b55b-5f4fd6ffaf1d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7513592-2f23-4ca1-b244-4d6c5a82db55","agentId":"adda18087b10e0b3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWXCcvfEmFHyjAftEBChvS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ccp_xstate\n2\t\n3\tThe v2 harness, rebuilt on XState. This file is a map, not the manual: standing knowledge lives in `docs/` and\n4\t`plan/`, where it can be checked. Keep this file under 100 lines, and keep every path it names real.\n5\t\n6\t## Principles\n7\t\n8\t- **The verifier proves it, not the builder.** An item is done when a separate session shows its outcome holds\n9\t  (`plan/README.md`, \"How slop is kept out\").\n10\t- **The why travels with the work.** Every change names its plan item; the item's prose holds the reasoning.\n11\t- **A working small system first** (Gall's Law), end to end before wide, root cause over symptom.\n12\t- **Step back, don't grind.** An item's `step_back` caps its rounds; past that, replan instead of retrying.\n13\t- **Decide two-way doors and write them down** in `plan/decisions/`. One-way doors (settings, secrets,\n14\t  anything outside this repo and the scratch repo) go in `plan/decisions/waiting-for-person.md`.\n15\t\n16\t## Branches and PRs\n17\t\n18\t- Name a branch `<kind>/<item-id>`, where kind is the item's kind: `build/journal-schema`,\n19\t  `probe/probe-platform-baseline`. Other work uses `replan/<item-id>`, `docs/<topic>` or `chore/<topic>`.\n20\t  No `claude/` prefix.\n21\t- One plan item per PR. Put `Item: <item-id>` on its own line in the PR body.\n22\t- Every commit ends with a `Claude-Session:` trailer naming the session that wrote it.\n23\t- Merge into `main` only when `ci` and `verdict` are green at the head sha. See `docs/gates.md`.\n24\t- After merging a plugin change, release it: `node scripts/release/release.mjs branch --push` (`docs/gates.md`).\n25\t\n26\t## Layout\n27\t\n28\t| Path | What |\n29\t|---|---|\n30\t| `plan/` | The plan: items, stages, ledger, cases, decisions. Start at `plan/README.md` |\n31\t| `plan/check.mjs` | Checks the plan; `--order` prints build order |\n32\t| `packages/` | npm workspaces for the harness libraries; `packages/journal/` is the record format, `packages/engine/` loads and hosts workflows and runs their effects |\n33\t| `workflows/` | Workflow files as XState JSON; `workflows/quick-fix.json` is the first |\n34\t| `plugins/` | npm workspaces for the Claude Code plugins |\n35\t| `verify/<item>/` | The verifier's tests and `verdict.json` for each item |\n36\t| `scripts/gates/` | The PR gates CI runs |\n37\t| `scripts/tournament/` | The generic design-tournament runner, args builder, measure and CI template (`docs/tournaments.md`) |\n38\t| `scripts/bench/`, `bench/` | The stage bench: run one model stage alone on fixed cases, score and compare prompts (`docs/prompts.md`) |\n39\t| `tournaments/` | One folder per design tournament, indexed in `tournaments/README.md`; lane code stays in the scratch repo |\n40\t| `test/` | Repo-wide tests, such as the workspace rules |\n41\t| `infra/cloud-environment/` | The cloud environment's setup script |\n42\t| `vendor/` | Third-party tools copied in verbatim; `vendor/documentation-downloader/` is the docs skill setup installs |\n43\t| `.github/workflows/` | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `.github/workflows/verdict.yml` |\n44\t| `docs/` | Standing knowledge; `docs/layout.md`, `docs/gates.md`, `docs/journal.md`, `docs/prompts.md` and `docs/tournaments.md` |\n45\t\n46\t## Commands\n47\t\n48\t```\n49\tnpm test                 # node:test over test/, scripts/, packages/, plugins/ and verify/\n50\tnode plan/check.mjs      # the plan check; CI runs both on every PR\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\tNode 22 or later. Zero runtime dependencies except `xstate`.\n54\t"}]},"uuid":"4e90fb37-ee54-40b0-9087-84db1aaf678d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:21:24.489Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b40734c0-2c36-46f3-b55b-5f4fd6ffaf1d","permissionDecision":{